Hi Andy,

Thanks very much for the info. I can now see what I was doing wrong with trying to recreate the effect. Though I still seem to have the same problem..

I've recoded an example (below), which hopefully will show more clearly what I'm stuck on. I've run this a few times, and sometimes it gives the same occupancy estimate, and other times it's different. I've also included an example output below with the assigned variables used from the attached files y_dat.txt & y_dat1.txt

Not sure where I'm going wrong here.

thanks
Naveed

#create survey data for 6 different observers:
obs1 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.8, 0.2))
obs2 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.7, 0.3))
obs3 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.9, 0.1))
obs4 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.8, 0.2))
obs5 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.7, 0.3))
obs6 <- sample (c(0, 1), size = 130, replace = TRUE, prob = c(0.9, 0.1))

#combine survey data
y_dat <- data.frame(obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4, obs5, obs6)

#create data frame for using different observers as detection covariate
obs_no <- rep(c("obs1", "obs2", "obs3", "obs4", "obs5", "obs6"), times = 130)
cov_obs <- data.frame(obs_no) # obs

#combine into unmarked data frame
umf00 <- unmarkedFrameOccu(y = y_dat, siteCovs = NULL, obsCovs = cov_obs)

#run model
fm00 <- occu(~ obs_no ~ 1, umf00)

#alter order of surveys and run model
y_dat1 <- y_dat[, sample(1:6)]
umf01 <- unmarkedFrameOccu(y = y_dat1, siteCovs = NULL, obsCovs = cov_obs)
fm01 <- occu(~ obs_no ~ 1, umf01)

#check results
fm00
fm01

###############
#if I rerun the following code several times it gives me different occupancy estimates some of the time, but the same occupancy estimate at other times:
